{"id":"h090","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The claim is true under the standard historical account.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0065},{"text":"In September 1928 Fleming noticed a Penicillium mold contaminating a Staphylococcus plate had killed surrounding bacteria.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-0.0148},{"text":"Fleming recognized the antibacterial substance the mold produced and named it penicillin.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0075},{"text":"The 1945 Nobel Prize was shared by Fleming, Florey, and Chain, with Fleming credited for the original discovery.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.1074},{"text":"Fleming did not isolate, purify, mass-produce, or develop penicillin into a usable drug; Florey and Chain did.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.4,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.9286},{"text":"Florey and Chain are often considered essential to penicillin's development.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4137,"phi":2.4415},{"text":"Ernest Duchesne described the antibacterial effect of Penicillium in his 1897 thesis, before Fleming, but it was largely overlooked.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.4,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.0314},{"text":"The discovery is conventionally credited to Fleming's 1928 observation and identification of the substance.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-0.0218},{"text":"The objections concern later development and earlier overlooked observations, and only qualify Fleming's credit without overturning the attribution of the discovery.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.255}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"support